Realize the complete selected Environment, or continue the exact operation an interruption left behind. The plan is always complete; --stage only gates which blocks this invocation starts, and the operation pauses at that boundary. Review the plan before confirming; --yes skips ordinary confirmation.

Usage:
  bootwright apply [flags]

Examples:
  bootwright apply --context lab --stage machines

Flags:
      --authorize stringArray   Acknowledge a planned risk (data-loss) (values: data-loss)
      --stage string            Select comma-separated stages to start (default: all) (values: controller, infra-components, substrates, machines, clusters, add-ons)
      --yes                     Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

Global Flags:
      --context string             Select a context (default: current context)
  -h, --help                       Show help for this command
      --ssh-ask-sudo-password      Request the borrowed account's sudo password
      --ssh-id-file string         Offer an explicit private key for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user string            Borrow an explicit POSIX account for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user-for-provisioned   Extend the borrowed account to provisioned machines
